{"events":[{"id":12262,"global_id":"bikeleague.org?id=12262","global_id_lineage":["bikeleague.org?id=12262"],"author":"7","status":"publish","date":"2023-05-05 14:01:19","date_utc":"2023-05-05 18:01:19","modified":"2023-05-05 14:01:19","modified_utc":"2023-05-05 18:01:19","url":"https:\/\/bikeleague.org\/calendar\/bike-advocacy-essentials-how-to-write-a-letter-to-the-editor\/","rest_url":"https:\/\/bikeleague.org\/wp-json\/tribe\/events\/v1\/events\/12262","title":"Bike Advocacy Essentials: How to Write a Letter to the Editor","description":"<p>How often have you read an article about a transportation issue in your community and thought, &#8220;why didn&#8217;t they include anything about biking?&#8221; People like you know how the current state of bicycling in your city\/town affects the entire community and a letter to the editor is a powerful tool for ensuring your voice is heard!<\/p>\n<p>In March 2023, the League hosted the \u201cBike Advocacy Essentials: How to Write a Letter to the Editor\u201d webinar to discuss guidelines and resources for writing an engaging and compelling letter to the editor.\u00a0 Sara Kiesler, former journalist and communications and marketing director at Cascade Bicycle Club, joined us to give you the nuts and bolts of this crucial advocacy tool.<\/p>\n<p>Find the <a href=\"https:\/\/bikeleague.org\/webinar-replay-how-write-letter-editor\/\">recap of the webinar on our blog<\/a>, or watch the video on YouTube below.<\/p>","excerpt":"","slug":"bike-advocacy-essentials-how-to-write-a-letter-to-the-editor","image":false,"all_day":false,"start_date":"2023-03-03 14:00:00","start_date_details":{"year":"2023","month":"03","day":"03","hour":"14","minutes":"00","seconds":"00"},"end_date":"2023-03-03 15:00:00","end_date_details":{"year":"2023","month":"03","day":"03","hour":"15","minutes":"00","seconds":"00"},"utc_start_date":"2023-03-03 19:00:00","utc_start_date_details":{"year":"2023","month":"03","day":"03","hour":"19","minutes":"00","second